on {:value "130552"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "131644"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "132724"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "133464"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "134052"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "263689"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "332092"} "2012"] "\n" [:option {:value "19009329"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2007828"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/659"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Welterweight, Greco-Roman (≤66 kg), Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "16 August 2016"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/902"} "Arena Carioca 2, Parque Olímpico da Barra, Barra da Tijuca, Rio de Janeiro"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/355542"} "18 from 18 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single elimination tournament. Competitors losing to the finalists entered repechage tournament for bronze medals."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The three most recent World champions at this weight (" [:a {:href "/athletes/123207"} "Frank Stabler"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/134990"} "Ryu Han-Su"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/107660"} "Davor Štefanek"] "), the finalists from the last Olympic Games (" [:a {:href "/athletes/122822"} "Omid Norouzi"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/117165"} "Tamás Lőrincz"] ") and the World champion (" [:a {:href "/athletes/132627"} "Rəsul Çunayev"] ") from the weight above were all competing in this weight class. Add in " [:a {:href "/athletes/132445"} "Migran Arutyunyan"] ", and fans were hoping for a dream quarter-final, depending on the draw."] "\n\n" [:p {} "But after all the rounds, it was the three-time Olympian " [:a {:href "/athletes/107660"} "Davor Štefanek"] " - who never even won an Olympic match previously (but was the 2014 World champion and the 2015 bronze medalist) - who reached the gold medal final against Armenian " [:a {:href "/athletes/132445"} "Migran Arutyunyan"] ", the 2015 European Championships silver medalist. The match ended in a 1-1 tie, with Štefanek getting the win on criteria because he was the last one to be awarded a point, thereby beating Arutyunyan, and celebrating with a backflip. Štefanek had won Serbia’s first medal in Rio after 11 medal-less days (and their second ever) and leading the Serbian team to their most successful Olympics as an independent nation."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The 66 kg bronze medals were won by 2014 World Junior champion and 2016 European Championships bronze medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/134103"} "Shmagi Bolkvadze"] " of Georgia, and 2015 World and European Games champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/132627"} "Rəsul Çunayev"] " of Azerbaijan."] "\n\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Fall", :class "footnote"} "VF"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Victories by Technical Superiority", :class "footnote"} "ST"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points", :class "footnote"} "TP"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Technical Points Received", :class "footnote"} "TPR"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/107660"} "Davor Štefanek"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SRB"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SRB.png"}] "SRB"]] [:td {} "15"] [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "1